messages:   13%|#3        | 78/600 [00:31<02:47,  3.12it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nCollege student Xiao Wang took the Postgraduate Admission Test exam in four subjects: politics, English, major one, major two. The sum of the scores of political and professional subject one is equal to the sum of the scores of the other two subjects.The sum of the scores of the political and professional subjects two is greater than the sum of the scores of the other two subjects. The scores of the professional subject one are higher than the sum of the scores of the political and English subjects.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above conditions, which of the following is the correct ranking of Xiao Wang's four subjects from high to low?\n# Options:\nA) Major subject one, major subject two, english, politics.\nB) Major subject two, major subject one, politics, english.\nC) Major subject one, major subject two, politics, english.\nD) Major subject two, major subject one, english, politics.. I think the correct option is: C\n", "To solve this problem, let's break down the given information and analyze each condition step by step.\n\nLet's denote the scores of the subjects as follows:.\n- Politics: P.\n- English: E.\n- Major one: M1.\n- Major two: M2.\n\nGiven conditions:.\n1. The sum of the scores of political and professional subject one is equal to the sum of the scores of the other two subjects.\n   - P + M1 = E + M2.\n\n2. The sum of the scores of the political and professional subjects two is greater than the sum of the scores of the other two subjects.\n   - P + M2 > E + M1.\n\n3. The scores of the professional subject one are higher than the sum of the scores of the political and English subjects.\n   - M1 > P + E.\n\nNow, let's analyze these conditions to determine the ranking of the subjects from high to low.\n\nFrom condition 1:.\n- P + M1 = E + M2.\n  This implies that the sum of the scores of politics and major one is equal to the sum of the scores of English and major two.\n\nFrom condition 2:.\n- P + M2 > E + M1.\n  This implies that the sum of the scores of politics and major two is greater than the sum of the scores of English and major one.\n\nFrom condition 3:.\n- M1 > P + E.\n  This implies that the score of major one is greater than the sum of the scores of politics and English.\n\nLet's use these conditions to deduce the ranking:.\n\n1. From condition 3, we know that M1 is greater than the sum of P and E. This suggests that M1 is likely the highest score among the four subjects.\n\n2. From condition 2, we know that P + M2 is greater than E + M1. Since M1 is already the highest, M2 must be higher than E to satisfy this condition. This suggests that M2 is the second-highest score.\n\n3. Now, we need to determine the ranking between P and E. Since M1 is greater than P + E, and M2 is greater than E (to satisfy P + M2 > E + M1), it is reasonable to assume that P is higher than E.\n\nTherefore, the ranking from high to low is:.\n- Major one (M1).\n- Major two (M2).\n- Politics (P).\n- English (E).\n\nBased on this analysis, the correct option is:. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
