rule of law.\n   - The passage concludes by stating that the proper functioning of the original supervision mechanism is an urgent issue.\n\n2. **Option Analysis:**.\n   - **Option A:** "The society ruled by law cannot mainly rely on the network for effective supervision.".\n     - This option aligns with the passage\'s emphasis that network supervision should not become the primary method of supervision in a society under the rule of law.\n   - **Option B:** "The network has more advanced supervision ability than other supervision mechanisms.".\n     - While the passage does mention that the network shows an advanced trend in supervision, this is not the main idea. It is more of a supporting detail.\n   - **Option C:** "Network supervision can play a better role on the basis of self-improvement.".\n     - The passage does not discuss the self-improvement of network supervision or its potential to play a better role through such improvement.\n   - **Option D:** "An important way of supervision in today\'s society is network supervision.".\n     - This option contradicts the passage\'s main point that network supervision should not become the primary method of supervision.\n\n3. **Conclusion:**.\n   - The main idea of the passage is that while network supervision has its benefits, it should not be the primary method of supervision in a society governed by the rule of law. Therefore, the correct answer is:. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
