messages:   51%|#####     | 305/600 [02:24<08:57,  1.82s/it][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nTo reduce the frequency of ground collisions, Innovair will begin giving its ground crews additional training, at an annual cost of $500, 000. Although this will cut the number of ground collisions by about half at best, the drop in repair costs can be expected to be much greater, since __ .\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following most logically completes the argument? In a typical year, Innovair's airplanes are involved in 35 collisions while parked or being towed in airports, with a resulting yearly cost of $1, 000, 000 for repairs.\n# Options:\nA) Most ground collisions have been caused by the least experienced ground-crew members\nB) A ground collision typically occurs when there are no passengers on the airplane\nC) The additional training will focus on helping ground crews avoid those kinds of ground collisions that cause the most costly damage\nD) The $500, 000 cost figure for the additional training of ground crews includes the wages that those crews will earn during the time spent in actual training. I think the correct option is: B\n", "To solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to identify the option that best completes the argument by explaining why the drop in repair costs can be expected to be much greater than the reduction in the number of ground collisions.\n\nLet's analyze each option:.\n\nA) **Most ground collisions have been caused by the least experienced ground-crew members.**.\n   - This statement might explain why additional training could reduce collisions, but it does not directly address why the drop in repair costs would be greater than the reduction in collision frequency. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
