messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn most cases, writing poems and filling words is a process of mutual accommodation between language and emotion. It is unpredictable for a beginner to have what kind of feelings and choose what kind of sentence pattern to start with. But once he has a preliminary idea, he can always get appropriate help in the book Tang and Song Poetry Rhythms. He will know which words are suitable to express what kind of feelings, what kind of rhyme he should choose, and how to make rational use of certain rhetorical devices so as not to be fooled in the face of special syntax. If you have read enough ancient poems and have a certain sense of language, you will indeed be able to complete your first creation with the help of this book. It can not teach people to write amazing masterpieces, but with the greatest sincerity to prevent you from making all kinds of jokes.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings is the main content of this text?\n# Options:\nA) Tang and song poetry rhythms is suitable for beginners because of its rich tones\nB) Poetry creation is essentially a process of mutual accommodation between language and emotion\nC) Tang and song poetry rhythms provides a very good help for beginners\nD) The creator of poetry must have abundant emotion and high literary accomplishment. I think the correct option is: D\n', 'To solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the context and analyze each option step by step.\n\n1. **Understanding the Context:**.\n   - The context discusses the process of writing poems, particularly for beginners.\n   - It mentions that the process involves a mutual accommodation between language and emotion.\n   - It highlights the role of the book "Tang and Song Poetry Rhythms" in helping beginners understand which words to use, what rhymes to choose, and how to use rhetorical devices.\n   - The book is described as a helpful tool for beginners to complete their first creation, though it does not teach them to write masterpieces.\n\n2. **Analyzing Each Option:**.\n   - **Option A:** "Tang and song poetry rhythms is suitable for beginners because of its rich tones.".\n     - The context does not specifically mention "rich tones" as a reason why the book is suitable for beginners. It focuses more on the book\'s guidance on words, rhymes, and rhetorical devices.\n   - **Option B:** "Poetry creation is essentially a process of mutual accommodation between language and emotion.".\n     - While this is mentioned in the context, it is not the main content. It is more of a background statement about the nature of poetry creation.\n   - **Option C:** "Tang and song poetry rhythms provides a very good help for beginners.".\n     - This aligns well with the context. The text emphasizes the book\'s role in helping beginners understand and use language and emotion effectively in poetry.\n   - **Option D:** "The creator of poetry must have abundant emotion and high literary accomplishment.".\n     - The context does not emphasize that a creator must have abundant emotion and high literary accomplishment. It focuses more on the book\'s role in helping beginners.\n\n3. **Conclusion:**.\n   - The main content of the text is about the role of the book "Tang and Song Poetry Rhythms" in helping beginners with poetry creation. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
