messages:   60%|#####9    | 358/600 [02:50<02:33,  1.58it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAt Happywell, Inc. , last year the average annual salary for dieticians was $50, 000, while the average annual salary for physical therapists was $42, 000. The average annual salary for all Happywell employees last year was $40, 000.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, if the information above is correct, which one of the following conclusions can properly be drawn on the basis of it?\n# Options:\nA) There was no dietician at happywell last year who earned less than the average for a physical therapist.\nB) At least one happywell employee earned less than the average for a physical therapist last year.\nC) At least one dietician earned more than the highest-paid happywell physical therapist last year.\nD) There were more physical therapists than dieticians at happywell last year.. I think the correct option is: D\n', "To solve this logical reasoning problem, let's analyze the given information and each option step by step.\n\n### Given Information:\n1. The average annual salary for dieticians at Happywell, Inc. was $50,000.\n2. The average annual salary for physical therapists at Happywell, Inc. was $42,000.\n3. The average annual salary for all Happywell employees was $40,000.\n\n### Analysis of Options:. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
