that chemical pesticides with "high efficiency, low toxicity and low residue" can be used to control diseases and pests in pollution-free vegetables.\n   - This option is correct based on the given information.\n\n4. **Option D: Pollution-free vegetables can be eaten safely and will never hurt your body**.\n   - The context only mentions that the pesticide residue is lower than the allowable edible standard stipulated by the state. It does not guarantee that pollution-free vegetables will never hurt your body under any circumstances.\n   - This option is not necessarily correct.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct statements according to the definition provided are:.\n- B) Agricultural antibiotics are allowed.\n- C) Chemical pesticides can be used as long as they are efficient and low toxicity.\n\nHowever, since the question asks for a single correct option, and both B and C seem to be correct, we should choose the one that is most directly supported by the context without any additional assumptions. .\n\nTherefore, the most directly supported correct option is:. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
