d the likelihood of leaving when it gets noisy again increases.\n   - **D) Afraid to meet strangers and dare not go to the streets**: This fits the definition. Being afraid of strangers (a situation of unhappiness) leads to avoiding going to the streets (escaping the situation), and the likelihood of avoiding the streets when afraid of strangers increases.\n\n3. **Conclusion**:. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
