messages:   79%|#######8  | 472/600 [03:34<00:23,  5.40it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nProfessional socialization refers to the process in which individuals choose occupations according to social needs, master the knowledge and skills to engage in a certain occupation, and update and retrain their knowledge and skills after engaging in a certain occupation\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the followings belongs to professional socialization:\n# Options:\nA) Zhang, the canteen administrator, saw that translation talents were urgently needed in many fields. he studied in his spare time and worked in a company after obtaining the translation qualification certificate\nB) After joining the army, young zhang was assigned to the automobile class and learned exquisite car repair skills. after retirement, he opened a repair department himself\nC) Li, an accountant of a company,loved cooking and participated in a training class in his spare time to learn nutrition knowledge and improved cooking skills\nD) Chen, a laid-off female worker, accumulated rich knowledge and experience while raising children. later, she opened a kindergarten on the suggestion of her friends. I think the correct option is: B\n', "To solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to identify which option best fits the definition of professional socialization provided in the context. The definition includes three key points:.\n1. Choosing an occupation according to social needs.\n2. Mastering the knowledge and skills for that occupation.\n3. Updating and retraining knowledge and skills after engaging in the occupation.\n\nLet's analyze each option based on these criteria:.\n\nA) Zhang, the canteen administrator, saw that translation talents were urgently needed in many fields. He studied in his spare time and worked in a company after obtaining the translation qualification certificate.\n- This option fits the definition well. Zhang identified a social need (translation talents), mastered the necessary skills (studied and obtained a qualification certificate), and transitioned to a new occupation (worked in a company).\n\nB) After joining the army, young Zhang was assigned to the automobile class and learned exquisite car repair skills. After retirement, he opened a repair department himself.\n- This option does not fully fit the definition. While Zhang learned skills and used them later, the initial choice of occupation (joining the army) was not based on social needs but rather an assignment. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
