messages:   80%|#######9  | 478/600 [03:41<01:07,  1.82it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf you close all the wrong doors, truth will be shut out.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is closest to the meaning of the above judgement?\n# Options:\nA) If truth is shut out, it must be that you close all the wrong doors.\nB) Truth can not be shut out unless all the doors of wrong are closed.\nC) If the truth is not shut out, then the door to all wrong must not be closed.\nD) To accept the truth, we must reject wrong.. I think the correct option is: A\n', 'To solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the given statement and analyze each option in relation to it.\n\nThe given statement is: "If you close all the wrong doors, truth will be shut out.".\n\nThis can be interpreted as a conditional statement: If P (closing all the wrong doors), then Q (truth will be shut out).\n\nNow, let\'s analyze each option:.\n\nA) If truth is shut out, it must be that you close all the wrong doors.\n- This option suggests a reverse implication: If Q, then P. However, the original statement does not guarantee that closing all the wrong doors is the only way to shut out the truth. There could be other ways to shut out the truth. Therefore, this option is not necessarily true based on the given statement.\n\nB) Truth can not be shut out unless all the doors of wrong are closed.\n- This option suggests that the only way to shut out the truth is by closing all the wrong doors: If Q, then P. Similar to option A, this is not necessarily true based on the given statement because it does not rule out other possibilities for shutting out the truth.\n\nC) If the truth is not shut out, then the door to all wrong must not be closed.\n- This option suggests the contrapositive of the original statement: If not Q, then not P. The contrapositive of a conditional statement is logically equivalent to the original statement. Therefore, this option is correct.\n\nD) To accept the truth, we must reject wrong. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
