r chen, saying that clients would not have confidence in the company if they saw such a mess in your office every day.\n- This option describes a criticism from a superior about the state of an office. It does not directly involve the manager actively managing impressions.\n\nC) After hearing his classmates secretly say bad things about him, lin couldn't help but go up and beat him.\n- This option describes a reaction to negative comments, which is more about retaliation than managing impressions.\n\nD) Before the interview, in order to be hired, xiao li in the clothing, hairstyle and so on has made the careful preparation. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
